<title>POLAND: Polish construction rises 3.2 pct in August.</title>
<headline>Polish construction rises 3.2 pct in August.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction sales rose 3.2 percent in August, after rising by 7.4 percent in July, and were 15.5 percent higher than in August 1995, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>Construction sales rose 2.0 percent in the January-August period against a 13.8 percent rise in the same period of 1995.</p>
<p> POLISH CONSTRUCTION	  AUGUST	  JULY	AUGUST 1995</p>
<p> month/month pct change	 3.2	 7.4 (6.7)	    3.7</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		15.5	16.1(15.4)	   22.0</p>
<p>NOTES: Revised data in brackets. July 1996 had 24 working days, August 1996 had 23 working days and August 1995 had 22 working days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
